1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,418
April 2nd, 2011. Wankhede Stadium,

2
00:00:04,418 --> 00:00:05,159
Mumbai.

3
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:07,953
Twenty-eight years of waiting end with one swing of

4
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:08,574
the bat.

5
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:09,896
A six over long-on.

6
00:00:09,896 --> 00:00:12,469
He finishes unbeaten on ninety-one.

7
00:00:12,669 --> 00:00:15,030
This is the story of Mahendra Singh Dhoni.

8
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,187
It starts in Ranchi,

9
00:00:17,187 --> 00:00:20,379
in 1981, with a pump operator's son.

10
00:00:20,579 --> 00:00:22,767
At school he is a football goalkeeper,

11
00:00:22,767 --> 00:00:25,698
until a coach hands him wicketkeeping gloves.

12
00:00:25,898 --> 00:00:30,221
In 2001, he is collecting tickets at Kharagpur railway

13
00:00:30,221 --> 00:00:31,002
station.

14
00:00:31,202 --> 00:00:34,415
Evenings and weekends, he keeps hitting sixes.

15
00:00:35,165 --> 00:00:39,554
December 23rd, 2004. His first match for India,

16
00:00:39,554 --> 00:00:41,161
against Bangladesh.

17
00:00:41,361 --> 00:00:42,773
He is run out for nought.

18
00:00:42,973 --> 00:00:46,143
Four months later, he hits a hundred and forty-eight

19
00:00:46,143 --> 00:00:47,525
against Pakistan.

20
00:00:47,725 --> 00:00:50,907
Then in Jaipur, one hundred and eighty-three not out.

21
00:00:50,907 --> 00:00:52,900
A record for a wicketkeeper.

22
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:57,115
In 2007, he captains a young team at the

23
00:00:57,115 --> 00:00:58,976
first World Twenty20.

24
00:00:59,176 --> 00:01:02,057
The final against Pakistan comes down to the last

25
00:01:02,057 --> 00:01:02,588
over.

26
00:01:02,788 --> 00:01:04,499
India win by five runs.

27
00:01:04,699 --> 00:01:07,767
Then the 2013 Champions Trophy.

28
00:01:07,767 --> 00:01:10,277
No other captain has won all three.

29
00:01:11,027 --> 00:01:13,367
On August 15th, 2020,

30
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:15,612
he retires with an Instagram video.

31
00:01:15,812 --> 00:01:18,355
Three hundred and fifty one-day games.

32
00:01:18,355 --> 00:01:20,164
Over ten thousand runs.

33
00:01:20,364 --> 00:01:23,441
The ticket collector from Ranchi who finished a World

34
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:24,443
Cup with a six.
